    <channel>
        <title>ColorPickr</title>
        <item>
            <title>0.16.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:20:25 +0000</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/dhuet/colorbody-releases</link>
            <sparkle:version>11</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.16.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul><li><b>Quick Pick</b> (⌃⌥C) now uses the macOS magnifier: your screen stays live, click picks, Esc cancels. It needs no Screen Recording permission, so picking works the moment you install ColorPickr. A small card by the cursor shows what you picked, its name in plain words and the format it was copied in.</li><li><b>Precision Pick</b> (⌃⌥⇧C) is the frozen-screen picker, for 3×3 and 5×5 averages, pixel nudging and dragging an area into a palette.</li><li>Screen Recording permission is now optional. It powers Precision Pick, Screen Check and the color vision simulation.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/dhuet/colorbody-releases/releases/download/v0.16.0/ColorPickr-0.16.0.dmg" length="6213582" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="HHe0p7Xpj2gnoDlhDQk4BymX4YjFQVfd1I0QqNoR2fzUsjaf+OC36m6XweE3V9e3BK+MQRLLAo0dGWzZBa7FAA=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>0.15.4</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:04:32 +0000</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/dhuet/colorbody-releases</link>
            <sparkle:version>10</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul><li>Fixed: the picker could seem frozen when macOS kept another app in front. Your first click now picks right away, and Esc always closes the picker.</li><li>macOS&#x27;s own Screen Recording prompt and ColorPickr&#x27;s alert no longer appear at the same time.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/dhuet/colorbody-releases/releases/download/v0.15.4/ColorPickr-0.15.4.dmg" length="6191786" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="B6WzmCg2OLIEd7f5zzVDpk8lukyBGCGQEWuqsDYlqtVKpen0IafXYCa//3pYwBFYH18dNo0AAJFJJQXPHMhzAQ=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>0.15.3</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:37:46 +0000</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/dhuet/colorbody-releases</link>
            <sparkle:version>9</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul><li>Fixed: after you turned on Screen Recording, ColorPickr could keep asking for it. It now checks with macOS&#x27;s screen capture directly instead of trusting a status that can lag behind System Settings.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/dhuet/colorbody-releases/releases/download/v0.15.3/ColorPickr-0.15.3.dmg" length="6187863" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="B1xJzG8/UxXvDu7d1RWB6dOCRZVkanCU2EBiz2uFM5doOoKqsqWkX10/N9q6yeBLT/SzXsWYuadNU0DeJFlZAA=="/>
